node_modules/
dist/
site/dist/
site/dist-edge/
_site/
.vite/
*.local
.DS_Store

# The demo loop's raw capture tracks -- the scripted sender walkthrough
# (record-walkthrough.mjs) and the live session's laptop side
# (demo-session.mjs) -- plus the trimmed/cropped intermediates and the
# side-by-side sync preview fed to the HyperFrames compose step in
# docs/demo/loop/README.md. Only the finished loop outputs are committed
# (site/loop.mp4, site/loop.webm, docs/loop.poster.png).
docs/demo/loop/*.webm
docs/demo/loop/*-trim.mp4
docs/demo/loop/preview-sbs.mp4
docs/demo/loop/.frames/

# The HyperFrames compose project for the loop (scaffolded by /general-video).
# Its assets/ are copies of the gitignored trims above and its output is the
# three committed files; the project itself is a scratch build, not an artefact.
videos/

# scripts/check-layout.mjs writes a picture of every failing screen/viewport
# combination here and clears the directory on each run. They are a debugging
# aid for the run that produced them, not artefacts anything reads later --
# unlike docs/screenshots/*.png, which the README embeds and which are
# committed on purpose.
docs/screenshots/layout/

# The Tauri app. Cargo.lock IS committed on purpose -- this is a binary, not
# a library, so the whole point of a lockfile is to pin it (see CLAUDE.md).
#
# gen/ used to be ignored whole, on the argument that `tauri android init` /
# `tauri ios init` regenerate it from tauri.conf.json in one command and a
# committed copy would be a second source of truth for the same settings.
# That held while gen/ contained nothing but generated schemas. Phase 4 broke
# it: the Android build needs `<uses-permission android:name=
# "android.permission.CAMERA"/>` in gen/android's AndroidManifest.xml, and
# tauri.conf.json has no field that can express it -- so the delta lives only
# in gen/, and an ignored gen/ means every re-init silently drops the camera
# permission and the scanner stops working with no diff to explain it. The
# runtime permission request Android 6+ wants for a "dangerous" permission
# may yet need hand-written Kotlin in MainActivity, which is the same problem
# again and larger. A patch script that re-applied the delta after each init
# was the alternative; it just moves the second source of truth into
# scripts/, and it cannot carry a Kotlin file.
#
# So gen/ is committed source now, except schemas/ -- those really are
# regenerated on every build and nothing is ever hand-edited in them.
app/src-tauri/target/
app/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# tauri-build writes this from build.rs's AppManifest every build ("DO NOT
# EDIT" is in the file itself) -- fully reproducible from build.rs, so
# committing it would just be a second place the same fact could drift out
# of step.
app/src-tauri/permissions/autogenerated/
